ANNEX E
(Foreword and Clause 5) CRITERIA FOR STRUCTURAL SAFETY OF TALL CONCRETE BUILDINGS E-1  SCOPE E-1.1  This Annex covers the following design aspects of reinforced concrete (RC) buildings of height greater than 50 m, but less than or equal to 250 m. Generally, these requirements are based on prescriptive approach and covers the following design aspects of tall buildings:
a) Selection of appropriate structural system;
b) Geometric proportioning of the building;
c) Integrity of structural system;
d) Resistance to wind and earthquake effects; and e) Other special considerations related to tall buildings. PART C STRUCTURAL DESIGN — SECTION 5 STRUCTURAL CONCRETE
E-1.2  This Annex is not applicable for tall buildings located in the near-field of seismogenic faults. For the purposes of this standard, near-field is taken as 10 km (shortest distance) from a seismogenic fault. E-1.3  This Annex is applicable only for buildings that house 20 000 or fewer persons. E-1.4  This Annex may also be used for design of buildings of height equal to or less than 50 m. The provisions of this Annex will add value to the design of such buildings. However, this Annex is not applicable for design of buildings of height more than 250 m. E-1.5  This Annex addresses the following typical structural systems of tall concrete buildings:
a) Structural wall systems;
b) Moment frame systems;
c) Moment frame — Structural wall systems;
d) Structural wall — Flat slab floor systems with perimeter moment frame;
e) Structural wall — Framed tube systems;
f) Framed-tube system;
g) Tube-in-tube system;
h) Multiple tube system;
j) Hybrid system; and k) Any of the above with additional framing systems, for example, outrigger trusses, belt trusses and braced frames. E-1.6  This Annex shall be read along with all Indian Standards relevant to design and construction of buildings and structures. In case of conflict, clauses given in this Annex shall be applicable.

