17.4 Friction Grip Type Bolting
17.4.1  In friction grip type bolting, initial pretension in bolt (usually high strength) develops clamping force at
the interfaces of elements being joined. The frictional resistance to slip between the plate surfaces subjected to clamping force opposes slip due to externally applied shear. Friction grip type bolts and nuts shall conform to the accepted standard [C-6A(39)]. Their installation procedures shall conform to good practice [C-6A(15)].
17.4.2 Where slip between bolted plates cannot be tolerated at working loads/ strength limit states loads (slip
critical connections), the requirements of 17.4.3 shall be satisfied at service and strength limit states loads, respectively. However, the requirements of 17.4.4 shall be satisfied by all connections at the strength limit states.
